What is a database object? Name five common database objects.

A database object is a structure in a database that is used to store, manage, organize, or retrieve data.

Five common database objects are:

Table – Stores data in rows and columns.
View – A virtual table created from a SQL query.
Index – Improves the speed of data retrieval.
Sequence – Generates unique numeric values automatically.
Stored Procedure – A set of SQL statements stored in the database to perform specific tasks.